/-
# Perron/cross-tail producer for physical boundary self-smoothing

The literal physical action defect is

  |A_k - A_k P_k|.

`BF4PhysicalBoundarySelfSmoothingCrossTail` reduces its required relative
bound to exact finite-prefix checks and one division-free analytic tail.
The other quantitative field in that interface is the terminal squared
projective spread

  spread(P_k)^2 <= 257/256.

This file discharges that field from the existing AF/Faraut Perron estimate
at depth `46 * bits + 6`.  The resulting contract leaves only two genuinely
physical constructions: a positive boundary smoothing kernel with a
same-kernel Perron estimate, and a scalar majorant for `|A_k - A_k P_k|`
with a finite-prefix/cross-tail certificate.

Exact finite data may be generated by Rust, C, or Python, but every rational
inequality is consumed by Lean.  No external computation is trusted as a
proof.

No `Classical.*`, `native_decide`, `sorry`, custom axiom, choice, or
noncomputable declaration.
-/

